<<~ kanawai uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119`>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! I2 ~ the far agent's relay seat, built

The carrier (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane#/the-far-agent`>>) rules the model; this kit reads what stands in the code. The lane builds on I1 (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/i1-intent-lane`>>): the intent plane, its entries and its reader already stand, and the lane adds the grammar that lets an agent off every device of the face act on the plane, the seat that admits its entry, and the readers that check it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-model`>>

!! The model the lane enacts

* ''The agent holds its own key.'' It signs its `intent` with that key and never wears a session of the face. A session meets one face and one anchor and carries a hand that acts as the face (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands`>>); the agent acts as itself under a delegation the face signed, so no hand opens a session for it and no atom signs its entry.
* ''The relay's admission sits beside a session and never inside one.'' The relay seat signs under its own key, held in the vessel's cold `intent-relay-key` row (`intent-relay-key-store.ts`). The admission runs on the relay door's route, off the session socket, and neither reads nor writes a session table. The operator's enable, disable and status act (`lares intent-relay`) names a face by its ordinal against the unlocked faces and changes nothing the face signs.
* ''Delegation and revoke are plane entries.'' `INTENT_DELEGATION_DOMAIN` mints the grant: an agent key, a verb prefix, an argument policy and a causal bound (`until` or `asOf` naming a roster act), signed by the persona root at its epoch. A `delegate-revoke` entry voids it. A grant lives only at its lineage's current root epoch and reads `lapsed` past a retired one (`intent-delegation.ts`, `intent-read.ts`).
* ''Admission leaves the entry unchanged.'' The agent's entry lands on the plane with the agent's signature and the receipt rides beside it as a separate record under `INTENT_ADMISSION_DOMAIN`: the relay key, the entry cid, the delegation cid and the heads the relay judged against. A receipt lists as provenance and never changes an intent's status, `mayAct` or winner (`intent-admission.ts`).
* ''Admission decides on fresh authority.'' After the relay signs, `admitAgentEntry` (`face-intent-door.ts`) re-reads the persona records, KEL chain and frontiers, decides against the plane's current document with no await before the append, answers a refusal or a duplicate without touching the plane, and re-signs when the authority fingerprint moved. One queue per plane serializes submissions, so concurrent bytes draw one append and a second relay's duplicate writes a receipt only.
* ''The door is the gate's, ring-gated and off by default.'' `makeIntentRelayGate` (`intent-relay-door.ts`) stands on the sealed gate server under `INTENT_RELAY_ROUTE`, one route per enabled face; frames extend `GATE_FRAME` by the next unassigned tags and one message bounds at the Noise limit. Enablement rests in `intent-relay-faces.json` (a hot custody row; only the relay key rests cold) and a restart without it stands nothing (`intent-relay-ring.ts`, `intent-relay.ts`).
* ''Readers trust the relay for nothing.'' A device, the node reader and the browser reader verify agent, delegation, face, invocation and outcome from the plane alone; a receipt names an entry and nothing more, and a receipt under a valid relay key for an absent, revoked or out-of-prefix entry makes nothing act. A revoke voids a pending sibling and keeps an earlier outcome as revoked-after-acting. The browser package grew no listener.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-slices`>>

!! The slices, each red-first with its control and its known positive

# ''Delegation grammar and read ~ BUILT.'' `buildDelegation`, `buildDelegationRevoke` and `buildAgentIntent` mint and sign; `readIntentPlane` folds a grant's status (`live`, `revoked`, `lapsed`, `closed`, `awaiting`) and voids an agent intent past a revoke; the CLI carries `delegate`, `delegate-revoke` and `delegations`. Tests: `intent-delegation.test.ts`, `intent-delegation-read.test.ts`, `intent-read.test.ts`.
# ''Causal revoke and bound ~ BUILT.'' A revoke arriving first refuses on read; an act admitted before it stays recorded as revoked-after-acting; a bound waiting on an unknown roster frontier stalls execution.
# ''Ring, relay custody, door ~ BUILT.'' The key store, the ring, the gate and the relay service (`intentRelayService`). Reds: a face never enabled stands no path, an oversized sealed frame draws a refusal through a live `ws` dial, the at-rest row decodes to a sealed format with no plaintext key (`intent-relay-ring.test.ts`, `intent-relay-key-store.test.ts`, `intent-relay-door.test.ts`, `intent-relay.test.ts`).
# ''Admission and the independent readers ~ BUILT.'' `decideAdmission`, `admitAgentEntry`, `makeFaceIntentReader`, `loadIntentFace` and the real `resolveIntentRelayFace`, which flushes the repo before it returns a receipt. Reds: a foreign face, a signing gap, a flush failure after the append, a key rotation between key read and signing, an uppercase outer signer, a roster or KEL change learned while signing, a merged own receipt beside a revoke (`intent-admission.test.ts`, `face-intent-admission.test.ts`, `intent-relay-admission.test.ts`, `intent-agent-verify.test.ts`).
# ''The storm ~ BUILT.'' `intent-relay-storm.test.ts` runs twelve cases over real planes, the real custody key and live `ws` dials: a revoke before and after admission, a sleeper that merges a revoke, a failed append, two racing relays, a hostile receipt for an absent, revoked or out-of-prefix entry, an unknown frontier that advances, one agent key on two faces, canonical-JSON and Unicode substitution, and a restart that stands nothing without its enablement row. Each case pairs a CONTROL, and the throwing clock judges only the immediate caller of `Date.now`.
# ''The opener wires the relay ~ BUILT.'' The opener seats `intentRelayService` in its cell before the first gate sweep (`gateSweep`), refreshes it at each sweep and closes it on teardown; K19's `dropFace` and `lightFace` refresh it at once, so a locked sibling's route closes with the lock and a lit one stands again (the census reds first; the service test keeps the other face admitting). Red: the opener census fails on the commit before the wiring. The durable-reopen witness opens a real `Repo` over `DurableNodeFSStorageAdapter`, admits through `resolveIntentRelayFace`, drops the repo, reopens it and finds one entry and the same receipt, and a retry returns `duplicate`; a flush that throws answers `fault` and its receipt never returns to the caller (`intent-relay-wired.test.ts`).
# ''The composers prove the planes they register ~ BUILT.'' Both composers register a face's circles, identities, sessions and intents through `provenPlaneUrls` (`face-boot-proof.ts`), so the relay serves a face's plane only where the face's signed log names it; `resolveIntentRelayFace` and `loadIntentFace` read each anchored row alone, so a malformed sibling row leaves only its own face unread.
# ''The SharedWorker holder listens first ~ BUILT.'' The production entry registers its connect listener before it loads, buffers ports while it starts, and refuses each port by name (`holder-unavailable`) when the start fails; the worker census reads where a listener registers in execution order.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-fences`>>

!! What the lane keeps off

The hands spine's session files, K15's seed, identity, custody and carriage-key code, K19's per-face providers, the porch and `GATE_FRAME` stay untouched. The relay never writes a session table, an agent never receives an atom or a session, and the lane carries no clock: every read and admission passes with a throwing `Date.now`. The lost-reply case proves a repeated submission after a delivered receipt duplicates nothing and the durable-reopen case proves a flushed receipt survives a reopened repo; a relay killed with its reply in flight, and a storage write that fails partway, stay unwitnessed.

!!! Owed
* The plane's hardening under re-pin, re-target and growth stands at roadmap row `I3` (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane#/the-reds`>>): the admission's commit-boundary rechecks, the receipt's one head digest and the single-effect spend.

<<~/ahu>>

